cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Superdiffusion: a Lean 4 formalization of superdiffusion and anomalous regularization in self-similar random incompressible flows"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the main results of
  superdiffusion in self-similar random incompressible flows: the
  superdiffusive asymptotics of the effective diffusivity, the
  renormalization of the generator (Theorem B), the anomalous large-scale
  regularity theory (Theorem C), and the quenched power-law superdiffusivity
  of the diffusion process itself (Theorem A), built on the public
  CoarseGraining homogenization library and the public MarkovProcess library.
  The production library contains no sorry and no custom axiom; each of the
  three Mathlib-only comparator challenges contains one intentional
  statement-level sorry whose completed solution is checked separately.
type: software
